    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d341">

                <pb facs="0379" n="305" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg305"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/7702</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Serbian Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Michailovitch</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 12, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received November 13.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: The Royal Serbian Government, with
                    the intention to greet the entry of the United States into the war against
                    Germany, the common enemy, and to thank her for the financial help extended by
                    the Government of the United States to the Serbian Government for the successful
                    prosecution of the war, sends a special mission to Washington, which is to be
                    composed of Dr. Milenko Vesnitch, Minister Plenipotentiary in Paris, chief of
                    the mission; Mr. Sima Lozanitch, former Minister of Agriculture; General
                    Michailo Rachitch, representative of Serbian General Headquarters to French
                    General Headquarters; Reverend Nicolai Velimirovitch, representative of the
                    Serbian Red Cross; Lieutenant Colonel Nenadovitch; Captain Yovitchitch; and one
                    attaché of Legation.</p>
                <p>The mission will sail from France on November 17, for New York.<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d341-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>In communicating this to you, I place myself at your disposal for any further
                    information you may require.</p>
                <p>I beg to renew [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">L. Michailovitch</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d341-f1" n="1" xml:id="d341-f1-content">
                <p>By a note of Nov. 13 (unnumbered), the sailing date was changed to Nov. 24, and
                    in another note of Nov. 15 (unnumbered), the Minister stated that the mission’s
                    departure had been indefinitely postponed on account of the meeting of the
                    Inter-Allied Conference (File Nos. 763.72/7722, 7751). The mission arrived in
                    the United States, Dec. 20.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
